From: SwiftPili <359733720+haikiseven@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Package: consume the locally built libvlc.xcframework

scripts/build-libvlc.sh emits Vendor/libvlc.xcframework, but Package.swift
resolved libvlc from a published release asset instead, so a local build --
including the VideoToolbox AV1 module and everything in scripts/patches/ --
never reached consumers.

Point the binaryTarget at the local artefact. A path: target has no checksum, so
it also stops the manifest and the shipped binary from drifting apart.

Run ./scripts/build-libvlc.sh --ios-only before building any consumer.

diff --git a/Package.swift b/Package.swift
index 4bfba78..82e40ca 100644
--- a/Package.swift
+++ b/Package.swift
@@ -16,10 +16,12 @@ let package = Package(
     .package(url: "https://github.com/pointfreeco/swift-custom-dump", from: "1.3.3")
   ],
   targets: [
+    // Local build: scripts/build-libvlc.sh emits Vendor/libvlc.xcframework
+    // with the VideoToolbox AV1 module and every patch in scripts/patches/.
+    // A url:/checksum: target would silently pull the stock upstream binary.
     .binaryTarget(
       name: "libvlc",
-      url: "https://github.com/harflabs/SwiftVLC/releases/download/v0.10.0/libvlc.xcframework.zip",
-      checksum: "4ae6e8978b61d458080ac5dbcf1f412118bae1c250091b0f790fc65a847e960d"
+      path: "Vendor/libvlc.xcframework"
     ),
     .target(
       name: "CLibVLC",
